{"shortDescription":"Spot basis values for soybeans were mostly steady to weaker in the US Midwest on Monday, spot checks showed, reflecting scattered weekend harvest progress that steered fresh supplies to soy processing facilities.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cents/bu:NOTE: 0 = Option Price, UNC…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis values for soybeans were mostly steady to weaker in the US Midwest on Monday, spot checks showed, reflecting scattered weekend harvest progress that steered fresh supplies to soy processing facilities."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The spot basis plunged by 40 to 45 cents per bushel at crushing sites in Decatur, Illinois, and Lafayette, Indiana."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["But other processors continued to post sizable premiums for soybeans delivered this week, underscoring demand for immediate supplies after a slow harvest start."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Skies were clear in parts of the Midwest over the weekend and on Monday, enabling fieldwork to resume in some areas where soils were dry enough to support heavy equipment."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["However, forecasts called for more harvest-slowing rains this week in states like Iowa, where flood watches were in effect on Monday afternoon, and Illinois. The states are the top two US soybean producers."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The USDA's weekly crop progress report showed the US soybean harvest was 17% complete as of Sunday, but Iowa's progress was only 3%, lagging the state's five-year average of 17%."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Corn basis bids were steady to stronger on Monday, supported by similar shortfalls tied to harvest delays."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The USDA said the corn harvest was 18% complete natio